"{\"body\":\"Discovered by T46 #693, Local actual primary Codex / GPT\u002d6\u002dAstra / xhigh, T3 wN:p6. Severity Low; Documentation Gap. Source reviewed\u002dat d707c82ab8c48b674acc1f95a9571f0cb24d226a. No fix applied; root retains stream disposition. This reactive bug has no milestone or parent.\\n\\n## Literal trace and reader consequence\\n\\nAt that source, docs/audits/README.md:19 instructs auditors to use instruction files whose `applyTo` matches changed paths. The current canonical .claude/rules/instruction\u002dfiles.md:9,27,37\u201347 specifies `paths:`, including omitted\u002dkey/every\u002dsession behavior. The README\u2019s surrounding lines17\u201322 describe current audit practice. A literal reader can search for the wrong selector and omit applicable rules.\\n\\nREADME SHA25617269ce0820878e809890a9f737cd665c77d32ff07a20e779aed4fac1b745d79; instruction guide SHA256ca638c32b6bbf991c02a865b9c3ab19279416806e7baa0a320713989610da845. Evidence: docs/audits/2026_11_03\u002depic\u002dm6\u002drecords/02\u002dforward\u002daudit.md, stage\u002db/table.json finding_trace and stage\u002db/read\u002d00/stdout in feature/m6\u002drecords\u002d693.\\n\\n## Self\u002drefutation and existing owners\\n\\nThe canonical guide remains reachable, so this is Low documentary risk, not an observed runtime failure. Historical #314 comment5879416677 preserves old Copilot methodology; that explains provenance but does not make this current instruction correct. The accepted T39 46\u002doutcome bridge contains no correction for this key; its README release instruction correction is separate PL\u002d02/#1400. Targeted searches for applyTo and docs/audits/README.md returned only #314 and #693 respectively. Search scope is retained, not claimed exhaustive.\\n\\nAlready written: this documentation wrote no device/cloud state; no user\u002ddata migration is implicated. Historical receipts and author identities must remain unchanged.\\n\\nCan this be done on the VM? Documentary source comparison and current rule/record checks need no runtime. No device or guest behavior is claimed.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n\u002d [ ] A bounded committed source trace shows the current audit README names the actual `paths:` convention and every\u002dsession behavior consistently with instruction\u002dfiles.md.\\n\u002d [ ] The correction\u2019s rules/record checks pass, and its exact changed\u002dpath evidence proves historical receipts and source programs unchanged.\\n\\nNo source correction, Phase7 resolution or closure is authorized by this issue alone; T46 stops at D for root disposition.\",\"comments\":[],\"number\":1416,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Low: Audit README names the obsolete rule\u002dselection key\"}\n"
